      "text": "To find the number of positive divisors of 24, we first need to find its prime factorization. We can do this by expressing 24 as a product of prime numbers:\n\n\\[ 24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1 \\]\n\nThe formula to find the number of positive divisors of a number given its prime factorization \\( p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\) is:\n\n\\[ (e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1) \\]\n\nFor the number 24, the prime factorization is \\( 2^3 \\times 3^1 \\). Applying the formula:\n\n\\[ (3 + 1)(1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of positive divisors of 24 is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can list all the positive divisors of 24 and count them. The divisors of 24 are:\n\n\\[ 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 24 \\]\n\nThere are indeed 8 divisors. Thus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
