      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the number of positive divisors of the number \\(24\\), we start by finding its prime factorization.\n\nFirst, we divide \\(24\\) by the smallest prime number, which is \\(2\\):\n\\[\n24 \\div 2 = 12\n\\]\nNext, we divide \\(12\\) by \\(2\\):\n\\[\n12 \\div 2 = 6\n\\]\nNext, we divide \\(6\\) by \\(2\\):\n\\[\n6 \\div 2 = 3\n\\]\nFinally, \\(3\\) is a prime number, so we stop here. Thus, the prime factorization of \\(24\\) is:\n\\[\n24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\n\\]\n\nTo find the number of positive divisors, we use the formula that involves the exponents in the prime factorization. If a number \\(n\\) has a prime factorization of the form \\(p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k}\\), then the number of positive divisors of \\(n\\) is given by:\n\\[\n(e_1 + 1) \\times (e_2 + 1) \\times \\cdots \\times (e_k + 1)\n\\]\n\nFor \\(24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\\), the exponents are \\(3\\) and \\(1\\). Applying the formula, we get:\n\\[\n(3 + 1) \\times (1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of positive divisors of \\(24\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
